
PUTLIN(3F)          UNIX Programmer's Manual           PUTLIN(3F)

NAME
     putlin - write a string to a file

SYNTAX
     character*(L) line
     integer fileid
     call putlin(line, fileid)

DESCRIPTION
     _P_u_t_l_i_n writes the character string _l_i_n_e on the output file
     associated with _f_i_l_e_i_d.  The number of characters written is
     the length of _l_i_n_e.

     _F_i_l_e_i_d is the integer returned from a successful _o_p_e_n(3F) or
     _c_r_e_a_t_e(3F).

SEE ALSO
     create(3F), getlin(3F), open(3F)

AUTHOR
     Bruce Julian, U.S. Geological Survey, Menlo Park, California

